<Root>
  <DefaultMacro>
    <Major></Major>
    <Description>Rust Auto Upgrade to Stone Macro


Set Up: Place the hammer tool in your action bar in the specified slot (default is slot 4 in this macro).

Aim: Position your cursor over the building component you wish to upgrade to stone (e.g., walls, foundations, ceilings).
Activate Macro: Start the macro. The script will automatically
:
Equip the hammer.
Open the upgrade menu by right-clicking on the component.
Move the cursor to select the "Upgrade to Stone" option.
Confirm the selection to apply the upgrade.

Repeat: If you want to upgrade multiple components, keep the macro running or trigger it again as you move to the next component.




Requirements
Screen Resolution: This macro is optimized for 1920x1080 resolution. If using a different resolution, adjust the mouse coordinates in the macro to ensure proper menu selection
.
Hammer Tool Position: By default, the hammer should be in slot 4 of the action bar. Change this in the macro script if your hammer is in a different slot.</Description>
    <Comment>https://keyran.net - Free macros download | Скачать бесплатные макросы </Comment>
    <GUIOption>
      <RepeatType>0</RepeatType>
    </GUIOption>
    <KeyUp>
      <Syntax></Syntax>
    </KeyUp>
    <KeyDown>
      <Syntax>KeyDown 33 1
Delay 200 ms
KeyUp 33 1
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 650 500
Delay 100 ms
RightDown 1
Delay 150 ms
LeftDown 1
Delay 50 ms
LeftUp 1
Delay 1 ms
RightUp 1
Delay 1 ms</Syntax>
    </KeyDown>
    <Software>Rust</Software>
  </DefaultMacro>
</Root>